WEBVTT

00:00:00.289 --> 00:00:04.035
Have you ever done something that is really difficult —

00:00:04.055 --> 00:00:08.956
and watched everyone treat it like it was EASY?

00:00:08.976 --> 00:00:12.135
You solved a serious cross-department problem.

00:00:12.155 --> 00:00:15.783
But everyone else saw ONE SMALL TASK.

00:00:15.803 --> 00:00:21.089
Many new managers believe good work speaks for itself.

00:00:21.109 --> 00:00:23.732
IT DOESN'T.

00:00:23.752 --> 00:00:26.657
And this isn't about bragging.

00:00:26.677 --> 00:00:35.711
In large companies, people see only a COMPRESSED version of reality from a few sources.

00:00:35.731 --> 00:00:41.108
You understand the dependencies, the escalations, and the root causes.

00:00:41.128 --> 00:00:44.916
But each leader sees only ONE FRAGMENT.

00:00:44.936 --> 00:00:47.364
Nobody sees THE WHOLE SYSTEM.

00:00:47.384 --> 00:00:50.701
Fixing the problem is only the first step.

00:00:50.721 --> 00:00:59.287
You also need to convert the value you created into ORGANIZATIONAL MEMORY.

00:00:59.307 --> 00:01:03.357
In the right forum, explain what broke,

00:01:03.107 --> 00:01:06.023
why it mattered, what changed,

00:01:06.043 --> 00:01:08.144
and why it WON'T HAPPEN AGAIN.

00:01:08.164 --> 00:01:11.428
You are not exaggerating the impact.

00:01:11.448 --> 00:01:13.877
You are making the full picture VISIBLE.

00:01:13.877 --> 00:01:18.999
When the organization understands and remembers your impact,

00:01:19.019 --> 00:01:21.714
you earn TRUST.

00:01:21.734 --> 00:01:27.650
The trust becomes the capital to solve the next, BIGGER problem.

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:32.185
You grow. And your team grows with you.
